blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<img width=\"1219\" height=\"772\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1253dbbf-7311-478a-8e09-a43685404f20\" />\n\n\n# Commit message pattern configuration not working per project\n\n## Description\nIn VSCode and Cursor, it is possible to define custom commit message patterns on a **per-project basis**.  \nFor example, I can configure whether commits should:  \n- Always be written in a specific language (e.g., Portuguese)  \n- Include icons in the message  \n- Automatically include the task/issue number  \n\nWhen I set these instructions in Cursor or VSCode, they are respected and applied correctly.  \n\nIn Trae, however, I tried setting the same kind of instructions in different places, but **none of them work**.  \nThe commit messages ignore the custom pattern.\n\n## Example\nIn Cursor, I can add this to `.cursorrules` or project configuration:\n\n[cursorrules.md](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22189501/cursorrules.md)\n\n<img width=\"1176\" height=\"481\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5338fd6d-b76c-42af-a2fa-bf0387389b7c\" />","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/1465/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/1465/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},"comments":[]}